cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use aqlab in work you cite, please cite it as below."
title: "aqlab: Arabic and RTL localization for Android APKs"
abstract: >-
  A command-line tool that makes an Android application Arabic and RTL-correct.
  It sets android:supportsRtl, migrates legacy left/right layout attributes to the
  logical start/end equivalents, scaffolds and applies a translation table, and
  lints Arabic string resources for Unicode bidirectional hazards, escaping bugs and
  format-specifier drift. Single file, Python standard library only.
type: software
